# Story 97: Remote Control (45s)
# Hook: In control mode you don't just watch -- you can drive the remote pane yourself.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-097-remote-control.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
In control mode you don't just watch -- you can drive the remote pane yourself.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and double-Escape into rysh mode. First we subscribe to a share in control mode.

[00:09.0 --> 00:17.0]
##upstream subscribe with control requests two-way access. The owner shared it as control, so commands are allowed.

[00:17.0 --> 00:27.0]
##upstream send pushes text to the remote pane. The server validates you're a subscriber and checks the blocklist first.

[00:27.0 --> 00:37.0]
Want to run a rysh command on the source pane? Prefix it with four hashes -- ####pane info runs ##pane info remotely.

[00:37.0 --> 00:42.0]
If the owner set command_approval, each command waits for their yes before it executes. Safety stays with the pane's owner.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Control mode turns a remote share into true pair programming -- gated by the owner's rules.

